{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>When they commit any sin of a man.</b> This passage concerns robbery of a convert, and the passage in Leviticus concerns robbery of an Israelite, as it is written there: וכחש בעמיתו. The passage of sacrilege is juxtaposed to the passage of the zav and the metzora, to teach you that zav and tzaraat come by way of sacrilege and sin." "<b>And that soul shall bear its guilt.</b> And they shall confess — Rabbi Natan says: this is a general principle for all those who are liable to bring a sacrifice, that they require confession."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:32.807234425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}